Create a professional presentation that explains the attached research paper, "Self-Improvement Memory Enables Continual Recursive Self-Improvement".

Scope:
- Explain only the paper. No general AI background slides, no company-specific or integration slides.

Cover, in this order:
1. Title slide (paper title, authors, affiliations, arXiv ID)
2. The problem: why an evolved harness can fail after a model or benchmark change (include the 68.41 vs 73.89 and 72.92 vs 75.72 examples)
3. Key definitions: harness, harness optimization (RSI), Continual RSI (CRSI), Self-Improvement Memory (SIM)
4. Method: the optimization loop (evaluator, proposer, selector), with a simple architecture diagram
5. SIM: what it stores (each JSON field), how it is updated each round, how the proposer and selector use it
6. End-to-end flow diagram: source RSI → carry harness + SIM → target RSI → held-out evaluation
7. Experimental setup: four domains, benchmarks, models, budgets, evolve/held-out split
8. The four comparison conditions
9. Results: cross-dataset table, cross-model table, the 10-run paired study (9/10, +2.36, p = 0.003), and other findings (model generations, shared harness, source retention)
10. Case study: the P5 → P8 completion-gate example, and the four roles of SIM
11. What transfers vs what needs revision
12. Limitations and ethics
13. Summary slide with key takeaways

Rules:
- Use only numbers and facts from the paper. Do not invent anything.
- Plain white background, minimal design, one idea per slide, short bullet points, no clutter.
- Use tables for results and simple box-and-arrow diagrams for the architecture and flow.
- Add speaker notes to every slide explaining the slide in simple language for someone new to the topic.
- About 15–18 slides.
